## Going-forward rules (index)

Each rule = one-line trigger + canonical doc pointer. Body lives in
the canonical doc.

### Code & design

- **Structural fix preferred when bug class can recur** (2026-05-09) — `CLAUDE.md § Design philosophy` (Maintenance gradient); `DESIGN_SPECS/meta-disciplines/structural-fix-preferred-decision-framework.md`. Trigger: same pattern at multiple sites drifted apart → registry/helper-extract with compile-time enforcement.
- **Framework discipline over ad-hoc per-instance code when recurrence is foreseeable** (2026-05-14) — `CLAUDE.md § Design philosophy` (Maintenance gradient — framework-driven); `DESIGN_SPECS/meta-disciplines/pattern-codification-lifecycle.md`. Trigger: ≥2 future applications projected AND bug class can recur AND framework cost ≤ projected savings × N → invest upfront.
- **Framework-driven CLI binary pattern Stage 4 cohort migration deferred to v5.16+ FOREACH_CLI_MODE** (2026-05-27 PM) — `DESIGN_SPECS/refactor-patterns/framework-driven-cli-binary-pattern.md` Stage 2 DRAFT v1.1 § "Pattern status update (2026-05-24)"; `plans/_future/2026-05-12-decoupling-endgoal-roadmap.md` "Training entry points" axis. Trigger: any plan body proposing framework-driven CLI binary application (per-core override emission CLI / schema migration CLI / similar standalone-binary cross-tool shape) at v5.15. Pattern's first canonical (`tools/stamp_model_cli.cpp` at `.B.3` Phase L) was REVERTED per YAGNI 2026-05-24 — operator workflow already covered by foxml_suite in-process stamping + boot log + GUI panels; v5.16+ FOREACH_CLI_MODE registry (TECH_DEBT-034) is the natural Stage 3 first canonical surface. **DO NOT** propose framework-driven CLI binary plans at v5.15; defer to v5.16+ decoupling endgoal context. Worked example: `.C` per-core override emission CLI SKIPPED at 2026-05-27 PM post-`.B.8` pickup re-scope; pipeline collapsed `.C` slot to `.D` direct. Sister to `feedback_overengineering_boundary_when_future_easier` + `feedback_no_defer_for_effort` (defer here is structurally justified by YAGNI revert + decoupling-endgoal alignment, not effort-avoidance).
- **Boundary-stable refactors over wide cascades** (2026-05-06) — `feedback_reduce_touch_sites.md`. Trigger: refactor crosses ≥4 files → propose stable boundary first.
- **Cohort-audit when new cfg field has 2+ siblings** (2026-05-11) — `DESIGN_SPECS/refactor-patterns/cfg-flag-eligibility-criteria.md`. Trigger: new boolean cfg field with 2+ semantic siblings → audit cohort.
- **Categorical applicability for new cfg fields** (2026-05-14) — `DESIGN_SPECS/framework-patterns/categorical-tag-applicability-pattern.md`. Trigger: new cfg field → fill applies_to_* columns; no hardcoded enum names in gating.
- **Cross-file cfg surfaces use `lives_in_struct`** (2026-05-14) — same doc § Cross-file. Trigger: cfg field in non-default cfg file → tag with `lives_in_struct` enum.
- **Bitmap overflow static_assert is mandatory** (2026-05-14) — `DESIGN_SPECS/refactor-patterns/bitmap-overflow-protection-discipline.md`. Trigger: any FOREACH_X-paired bitmap field → co-located `static_assert(COUNT <= sizeof(type)*8)`.
- **Type-trait dispatch via `tt::` namespace for typed registry dispatchers** (2026-05-14) — `CLAUDE.md H13` (invariant); `DESIGN_SPECS/framework-patterns/type-trait-dispatch-via-tt-namespace.md`. Trigger: building registry-driven dispatcher → use `tt::<verb>_field<T>` with destination-by-reference + type-family static_assert. NEVER `*reinterpret_cast<X*>(...)` punning.
- **Multi-bit state encoding for K-state fields (K = 2..16)** (2026-05-13) — `DESIGN_SPECS/refactor-patterns/multi-bit-state-encoding-pattern.md`. Trigger: new K-state field → N-bit packed slot (N=ceil(log2 K)) + branchless inference API.
- **Cfg↔ML surface-alignment audit at every ML feature add** (2026-05-14) — RECURRING_BUG_PATTERNS Class 24; `CLAUDE.md § Design philosophy` (Maintenance gradient). Trigger: new ML capability → answer 4 columns (cfg parse / Settings render / Stamp tag / Per-core override). Fire `/ml-audit` at sub-ship close.
- **Decision-time data binding for per-instance cfg values** (2026-05-15) — `DESIGN_SPECS/refactor-patterns/decision-time-data-binding-pattern.md`; Class 27. Trigger: subsystem needs cfg value at per-fill/event time → pre-resolve onto in-flight object at decision time. FORBIDDEN: scalar cfg-mirror field on subsystem state.
- **Registries optimize for ADDING; principle + sweep optimizes for ELIMINATING** (2026-05-15) — `DESIGN_PHILOSOPHY.md` § 1.5. Trigger: considering new registry → ask "should this pattern accumulate (registry good) OR shrink (registry counterproductive)?"
- **Branchless dispatch preferred for SP/HP data-dependent code** (2026-05-15) — `DESIGN_SPECS/refactor-patterns/branchless-dispatch-discipline.md`; Class 28. Trigger: data-dependent dispatch on SP/HP/drainer/producer code → fn pointer table / 2D state×type table / pre-resolve. Real-world mispredict is 30-100ns.
- **Audit hand-waves proactively when "branch is fine" framing surfaces** (2026-05-15) — same doc § "The hand-wave anti-pattern". Trigger: "branch is fine because predictor handles it" OR "mispredict is only 5-15ns" → STOP; re-examine through determinism + p99 lens.
- **Audit invocations specify scope per situation** (2026-05-15) — `DESIGN_SPECS/audit-methodologies/audit-scope-taxonomy.md`. Trigger: invoking audit skill → specify scope (current / wide / scoped <glob> / module:<name> / chain:<symbol>). Default `current`; reserve `wide` for quarterly + post-codification.
- **Multi-state dispatch with per-state metadata when N-state enum exhibits asymmetric behavior** (2026-05-16) — `DESIGN_SPECS/framework-patterns/multi-state-dispatch-with-per-state-update-metadata.md`. Trigger: dispatch enum has ≥3 states + behavior splits along ≥2 orthogonal axes → encode in X-macro row metadata columns; auto-compute dispatch tables.
- **Audit canonical sister before proposing new framework infrastructure** (2026-05-17) — `feedback_audit_canonical_sister_before_new_infra.md`; `DESIGN_SPECS/meta-disciplines/canonical-sister-extension-discipline.md`. Trigger: plan proposing new registry/bit/dispatch/sidecar/macro → grep codebase for canonical sister patterns FIRST; if ≥50% overlap + same consumer behavior → EXTEND.
- **Framework-layer payoff has diminishing returns; stop at the inflection point** (2026-05-17) — `feedback_framework_layer_payoff_diminishing_returns.md`. Trigger: tempted to propose new framework layer past inflection. Recognition: sites-added-vs-eliminated (60:4 ship; 6:5 reject); walker iterating zero rows; audit catches small-duplication territory. Lifecycle: build (ARCHITECT bias OK) → consolidation (aggressive framework) → post-inflection (this discipline) → maintenance (code-moving wins). Phase transitions operator-signaled.
- **Proportionate response to audit findings** (2026-05-17) — `feedback_proportionate_response_to_audit_findings.md`. Trigger: audit catches structural issue. Surface full menu (A INLINE MERGE / B ACCEPT WITH RATIONALE / C FOLD / D ARCHITECT + NO-FOLD first-of-kind) + evaluate each honestly + pick what's actually right (not first sufficient; not smallest). Audit catch is information; response is judgment.
- **Plan right, not fast** (2026-05-17) — `feedback_plan_right_not_fast.md`. Trigger: planning-grade decision. Planning IS the hard part of SWE in 2026; AI handles mechanical coding; human value-add concentrates in planning. Disciplines support decide-rightly, not decide-quickly. Indecisiveness is feature; speed heuristics undercut planning depth.
- **4-pillar self-audit before surfacing recommendations** — `feedback_audit_own_proposals_with_same_rigor.md`. Trigger: before surfacing ANY recommendation. 4 pillars: DESIGN_SPECS cross-check / anti-pattern catalog check / operator-impact / novel-alternative. `/readiness` Checks 31-33 verify. Sister memories: `feedback_recheck_designspecs_on_pushback`, `feedback_surface_operator_migration_path_proactively`, `feedback_proactive_novel_alternative_consideration`.
- **Future-headache vs optimization scope framework** — `feedback_future_headache_vs_optimization_scope_framework.md`. Trigger: scope discoveries during refactor/cleanup. Anti-pattern instance survival = close at ship; pure perf optimization = defer + document.
- **Iteration spiral as audit-meta-gap signal** — `feedback_iteration_spiral_signals_audit_meta_gap.md`. Trigger: plan body amendments find smaller-and-smaller findings across 4+ cycles. STOP individual-finding-chase; codify META-gap immediately per `DOCS/DESIGN_PHILOSOPHY.md` § 11.5 procedure; verify inflection. Common meta-gap shapes: consumer enumeration / cross-pattern access / cross-file-type / sister-registry / naming-asymmetry.
- **Comprehensive consumer enumeration before registry-row deletion** — `feedback_enumerate_consumers_before_registry_row_deletion.md`. Trigger: plan proposes X-macro registry row deletion / rename / column-1-vs-source-name change. Run ONE comprehensive grep covering all access patterns across all file types BEFORE plan body lock. Sister: `feedback_audit_canonical_sister_before_new_infra` (producer side; this is consumer side).
- **Implementation-detail audit layer (M4) above SHAPE** — `feedback_implementation_detail_blindspot_recovery_via_taxonomy.md`. Trigger: SHAPE audits return GREEN/YELLOW after 3+ iterations OR struct-gen migration crosses ≥2 registries OR type unification OR cross-registry consumer OR macro hoisting OR wire-format ordering change. Fire `/blindspot-scan` against the 12-category taxonomy at `DESIGN_SPECS/meta-disciplines/implementation-layer-blindspot-taxonomy.md`.
- **Framework-driven CLI binary for cross-tool wire-format surfaces (≥3 recurrence)** (2026-05-18) — `DESIGN_SPECS/refactor-patterns/framework-driven-cli-binary-pattern.md`. Trigger: cross-tool surface (typically `tools/*.sh`) emits wire format that mirrors engine emit; Layer 7 § cross-tool emit-site enumeration catches recurring drift (≥3 sync events) → STRUCTURAL FIX preferred over discipline-application. Replace bash with thin C++ CLI binary calling engine framework API directly (no mirror; drift impossible by construction). Sister: `wire-format-byte-preservation-discipline.md` Layer 7 (the DISCIPLINE; this rule is the STRUCTURAL-FIX upgrade); `feedback_structural_fix_for_recurring_class.md` (parent meta-rule); `feedback_no_defer_for_effort.md` (the rule that catches "bash patches at this ship → C++ migration later ship" as effort-deferral when same surface). Skip when: cross-tool surface lacks framework-driven C++ equivalent OR operator workflow needs bash-only OR recurrence count < 3.
- **B-Plus CI tool — compile-time plan body symbol verification at COMMIT layer** (2026-05-26) — `tools/check_plan_body_symbol_existence.py` + pre-commit hook at `.git/hooks/pre-commit` + `/readiness` Check 32. Trigger: any plan body .md edit (auto-invoked at commit time). Extracts ```cpp blocks, derives includes, compiles via g++, classifies failures (FABRICATION vs HARNESS-ISSUE). Bypass with `SKIP_PLAN_BODY_CHECK=1` env (use sparingly). Sister checks: Check 33 (M6 body-content arg enumeration); Check 34 (tiered-audit declaration). Parent memory: `feedback_verify_symbol_existence_at_plan_drafting_time` (Stage 6 cadence-locked); `feedback_structural_fix_for_recurring_class` (parent: structural enforcement beats memory codification alone — 6 NEW Class 14 fabrications introduced in-cycle AFTER M6 codification proved insufficient at v5.15.5.F.4d.1.B.4 v1.7.3→v1.7.4). Extend `SYMBOL_INCLUDES` / `CALLER_SCOPE_PREFIXES` / `KNOWN_HARNESS_FN_MISMATCHES` maps as new symbols/patterns surface.
- **`/capture-audit` skill — mechanical decision-capture drift check** (2026-05-26) — runs as pre-commit gate (via `/sync-workspace`) + pre-handoff gate (via `/handoff`) + standalone. 10 checks: MEMORY.md sync / plan body frontmatter (`audit_tier:` + `sister_specs:`) / decision-log artifact existence / sentinel matching (`<!-- D/C/F: <id> -->` + `<!-- STATUS: <state> -->`) / handoff doc currency (PENDING items vs git log) / Stage 6 promotion candidates per M7 / DESIGN_SPECS Stage 2→3 promotion eligibility / skill-in-CLAUDE.md-suite linkage (recursive trust anchor) / memory→DESIGN_SPECS sister cross-ref / CLAUDE.local.md going-forward rules currency. Exit 0=clean / 1=findings; `--strict` blocks. Sister: M7 parent (`structural-enforcement-when-memory-insufficient.md`); session decision log discipline (`feedback_session_decision_log_discipline`).
- **Session decision log discipline** (2026-05-26) — `feedback_session_decision_log_discipline.md`; template at `claude-skills/capture-audit/decision-log-template.md`. Trigger: planning cycle > 3 amendments OR multi-session ship. Per-version sidecar at `plans/<sprint>/decision-logs/<plan-name>-v<version>.md`. Captures Decisions (operator-decided) + Commitments (claude-said-will-do) + Discoveries (new findings) + STATUS (pending/landed/dropped/deferred). Plan body uses `<!-- D/C/F: <id> -->` + `<!-- STATUS: <state> -->` sentinel markers. `/capture-audit` Check 3+4 enforce. Closes rabbit-hole-amnesia failure mode. Sister: feedback_structural_enforcement_when_memory_insufficient (M7 parent); feedback_iteration_spiral_signals_audit_meta_gap (recognition trigger).
- **`/accept-handoff` skill — receiver-side handoff verification** (2026-05-26) — fresh-session pickup runs ONE command to: read handoff doc + load all "Critical pickup-time reads" files + run `/capture-audit --deep` (verify NO drift since handoff written) + run `/readiness` against in-flight plan body + read CLAUDE.md/local.md/MEMORY.md baseline + recreate TaskList from handoff Stage 1.5 capture + verify engine + workspace git state matches handoff claims + output PICKUP-READY status + concrete next-action. Closes "fresh session forgets to load required reading" failure mode. Sister to `/handoff` (writer side); `/capture-audit` (drift check at receiver-time).
- **Sprint sequencing — features first, then cleanup** (folded from memory 2026-05-26). Trigger: planning a sprint that mixes feature work with TECH_DEBT cleanup. Implement new features in the primary sprint; cleanup gets its own dedicated focused sprint (avoid mixing). Worked example: v5.x cycle keeps feature ships separate from cleanup ships (`.B.5-.B.11` file-size umbrella is dedicated cleanup AFTER `.B.4` train-serve feature work).
- **Multi-surface deletion ordering (B14 NEW pillar)** (2026-05-26 PM) — `feedback_multi_surface_deletion_ordering_discipline.md`; `DESIGN_SPECS/meta-disciplines/implementation-layer-blindspot-taxonomy.md` B14 pillar Stage 2 DRAFT. Trigger: deletion of feature/cfg/symbol spanning ≥3 files with compile-time interdependencies. Enumerate sites + classify per deletion-kind heuristic (operator-facing-doc / stale-comment / log-string / GUI-gating / test-surface / cohort-wrapper / DELETE-with-body / UNCONDITIONALIZE-body / enum-constant / cfg-field-row / archived-changelog LEAVE / current-changelog historical-row LEAVE) + sequence per leaves-first ordering (sites with no compile dependency first; sites consumed by others last; cfg-field-row LAST per H17 framework discipline). B-Plus v0.4 `--gen-deletion-cohort PATTERN` mechanizes; `/blindspot-scan B14` audit + `/readiness` Check 41 at audit-time enforce.
- **Unconditionalization latent assumption shift (B15 NEW pillar)** (2026-05-26 PM) — `feedback_unconditionalization_latent_assumption_audit.md`; `DESIGN_SPECS/meta-disciplines/implementation-layer-blindspot-taxonomy.md` B15 pillar Stage 2 DRAFT (1st instance only; Stage 3 promotion deferred to 2nd canonical per `feedback_proactive_novel_alternative_consideration`). Trigger: removing cfg-gate via "always-true" simplification (`if (cfg.X == VALUE)` → unconditional because VALUE is the only surviving value post-feature-deletion). Enumerate latent per-arch/per-mode assumptions in formerly-gated block; verify NONE are load-bearing for no-longer-existent cohort BEFORE unconditionalizing. `/blindspot-scan B15` audit + `/readiness` Check 42 at audit-time enforce.
- **Operator-facing doc cohort at cfg deletion** (2026-05-26 PM) — `feedback_operator_facing_doc_cohort_at_cfg_deletion.md`. Trigger: deletion of cfg field / operator-facing feature. Comprehensive sweep of operator-facing doc surfaces (README + DOCS/QUICKSTART.md + engine.cfg.example + sister operator-onboarding docs) included in deletion-cohort enumeration distinct from code-side consumer enumeration. B-Plus v0.4 generator includes `operator-facing-doc` kind classification; `/readiness` Check 43 at audit-time enforce.
- **Archived changelog preservation discipline** (2026-05-26 PM) — `feedback_archived_changelog_preservation_discipline.md`. Trigger: any deletion / refactor / cleanup touching `DOCS/changelogs/<old-date>-*.md` files OR archived rows in `DOCS/CHANGELOG.md`. DO NOT modify archived files; archived = timeless history. Only CURRENT CHANGELOG.md gets NEW row at ship close. B-Plus v0.4 excludes archived changelogs by default (`-g '!DOCS/changelogs/2026-04-*'`); operator opt-in via `--include-archived` flag for inspection only.
- **Deletion-scope classification at plan-draft time** (2026-05-26 PM) — `feedback_multi_surface_deletion_ordering_discipline.md` (sister to B14 codification); classification informs audit selection. Trigger: plan body proposes deletion-class scope. Classify deletion-scope at plan-draft time: SINGLE-FILE (no B14 needed; just delete) / CROSS-FILE (B14 applies; leaves-first ordering required) / CROSS-SURFACE-WITH-DOCS (B14 + sister operator-facing-doc cohort + archived-changelog preservation all apply). Classification drives which audit (B-Plus v0.4 + B14 + B15 + Check 41/42/43) fires at pre-coding gate. Sister to `feedback_tiered_audit_discipline_per_plan_scope` (parent meta-rule for audit tier classification).
- **Cfg field categorization at registry add time** (2026-05-27) — `feedback_cfg_field_categorization_at_registry_add_time.md`; `feedback_categorize_by_consumer_pattern_not_field_name.md`; `DESIGN_SPECS/framework-patterns/cfg-field-categorization-discipline.md`; `/readiness` Check 44; CI Check 8 sister. Trigger: any new cfg field row addition OR re-categorization migration OR cohort cleanup. Apply 4-category decision tree: PER_CORE_MODE_NO_FLAT_FIELD (each core explicitly picks; no uniform default; sister to `strategy` row) / PER_CORE_FLAT_SYNC_PARAMETER (uniform default + per-core override) / GLOBAL_ONLY (engine-wide; no per-core variation) / CFG-FLAG BITMAP BIT (BOOL semantic; H14 bit-packing). Field-name taxonomy NOT a substitute for consumer-pattern analysis — must verify via 5 mechanical questions: macro family / global manual struct field presence / walker behavior / consumer reads + scope / per-core override syntax. Re-categorization is 5-step atomic migration (partial migration creates orphan state worse than original). Sister-pattern co-location check required for `enable_X`/`use_X`/`X_enabled` patterns (grep MASK_*_X_ENABLED across all 5 cfg-flag bitmap domains). DOD audit at placement (H6/H14/H7/H20). First canonical at v5.15.5.F.4d.1.B.4 v1.7.6 Phase Cx-cfg-cohort (9-field GLOBAL re-categorization + 2 H14 violation closures).
- **C++17 inline-variable discipline for header-only shared state** (2026-05-27) — `feedback_cpp17_inline_variable_for_shared_state_across_tus.md`; `DESIGN_SPECS/data-disciplines/cpp17-inline-variable-for-header-shared-state.md` (Stage 3 first canonical). Trigger: any header-only global variable that needs shared storage across TUs (signal handler flags / test counters / cross-thread state) → declare with C++17 `inline` keyword. NEVER `static` (each TU gets own copy → silent shared-state corruption). NEVER extern+define-in-cpp (defeats header-only convention). 2 canonical applications landed at `.B.5` WIP-B1 + `.B.6` WIP-B3.
- **Single source of truth discipline** (2026-05-27) — `feedback_single_source_of_truth_discipline.md`; `DESIGN_SPECS/meta-disciplines/single-source-of-truth-discipline.md` (Stage 3 first canonical). Trigger: any fact/constant/struct/function body that exists in 2+ places → SSoT violation candidate. Default to MERGE unless semantic distinction matters (then document why separate). Composes with structural-fix discipline + canonical-sister discipline. First canonical at `.B.6` Decision H (drain_manual_closes LIVE + NO-OP merged into single function with #ifdef inside body).
- **Count code-LOC not total-lines for thresholds** (2026-05-27) — `feedback_count_code_loc_not_total_lines.md`; `DESIGN_SPECS/doc-disciplines/file-size-split-discipline.md` § "Threshold counting methodology". Trigger: any file-size threshold check / function length / complexity audit → count ACTUAL CODE LOC via `grep -vE '^\s*(//|\*|/\*|$)' <file> | wc -l` (exclude comments + blanks). Heavily-documented files shouldn't be penalized vs sparsely-documented ones of same code mass. Codified after `.B.6` B.4.1 revert (Run.hpp 2,436 total / 1,406 code — already under 1500 threshold by code-LOC).
- **Forward-decl at GLOBAL scope NOT inside namespace tt** (2026-05-27) — `feedback_forward_decl_at_global_scope_not_namespace.md`; RECURRING_BUG_PATTERNS Class 34; `DESIGN_SPECS/meta-disciplines/implementation-layer-blindspot-taxonomy.md` B17 pillar (Stage 2 DRAFT). Trigger: any monolithic-header subfolder split / header extraction / sub-file declaring forward-decls. Forward-decl `namespace tt { class X; }` creates SHADOW type tt::X distinct from ::X (compile error: "no member named 'X' in scope"). Prefer `#include <header>` over forward-decl for std:: types. 2 worked instances at `.B.6` Phase B (steady_clock + CandleAccumulator shadows).
- **Block-scope statics need explicit-arg passing when hoisting** (2026-05-27) — `feedback_enumerate_block_scope_statics_before_hoist.md`; RECURRING_BUG_PATTERNS Class 35; `DESIGN_SPECS/meta-disciplines/implementation-layer-blindspot-taxonomy.md` B18 pillar (Stage 2 DRAFT). Trigger: any lambda hoist / function extraction from monolithic header into different scope. Enumerate block-scope `static` variables in enclosing scope BEFORE writing hoisted signature; pass each as explicit fn arg (pointer for mutable; by-value for read-only). Composes with M6 parent discipline (`feedback_enumerate_helper_signature_args_before_extract`). Worked instance at `.B.6` Phase B.2 fan_out hoist (6 missed block-scope statics → final signature = 25 args).
- **Sister-cohort amendment completeness when amending Class catalog / DESIGN_SPEC / ledger** (2026-05-27) — `feedback_sister_cohort_amendment_completeness.md`; `DESIGN_SPECS/meta-disciplines/sister-cohort-amendment-completeness-discipline.md` (Stage 2 DRAFT v1.0 at .B.8). Trigger: any Class catalog / DESIGN_SPEC / ledger amendment proposal. Enumerate sister-cohort artifacts via (1) cross-refs IN amended artifact (sister_specs frontmatter / Cross-references / Sister classes), (2) reverse cross-refs FROM sister artifacts (grep across catalog + DESIGN_SPECS + ledger + skill + memory dirs); apply parallel amendments same ship. Recursion termination via fixpoint enumeration. AMENDMENT-layer sister to canonical-sister-extension-discipline CREATION layer. Worked example: .B.8 Phase D Steps D.4/D.5/D.6 (Class 27/25/18 sister-catalog amendments) + Phase H.2.d (/dod-audit sister-skill amendment). `/capture-audit` Check 9 + `/blindspot-scan` catch drift mechanically.
- **Forward-promise auto-write verification at next-ship time** (2026-05-27) — `feedback_forward_promise_auto_write_verification.md`; `/capture-audit` Check 11 (NEW v5.15.5.F.4d.1.B.8). Trigger: at ship-close + /handoff + next-ship pickup. Verify prior ship forward-promises (PARITY entries / TECH_DEBT / catalog amendments / DESIGN_SPEC Stage promotions / Stage 6 escalation candidates) landed at expected ledger location; surface UNFULFILLED for retroactive closure. Sentinels: "forward advisory" / "DOCUMENTED-RISK entry at .X close" / "Stage 6 escalation candidate at .X" / "auto-write at ship close: " / "queued for .X" / "deferred to .X". Mechanical enforcement at commit-time per /capture-audit --deep. Worked example: .B.8 Phase G Step G.6 retroactively closes .B.7 Class 26 catalog DOCUMENTED-RISK PARITY entry forward-promise (which was never actually written).

### Thread isolation between subsystems

- **GUI ↔ HP/SP thread isolation: NEVER share state directly** (2026-05-14) — `DESIGN_SPECS/framework-patterns/universal-registry-bitmap-dispatcher-pattern.md` § GUI ↔ engine. Trigger: new subsystem touching engine state from different thread → typed mirror per side; communicate via file + reload-signal; NEVER pointer-share. Aligns with H3.

### Process & sprint

- **Audit re-fire at substantive plan amendment** (2026-05-27) — `/precoding-audit-gate` re-fire when plan body substantively amended (architectural decision shift, scope reframing, categorization change, framework-pattern application question). Sister to feedback_iteration_spiral_signals_audit_meta_gap (recognition trigger: 3+ amendment cycles = audit METHODOLOGY gap) + feedback_audit_canonical_sister_before_new_infra (DESIGN_SPECS cross-ref before recommending) + feedback_recheck_designspecs_on_pushback (don't reactively flip on operator pushback) + feedback_operator_pushback_as_audit_signal (operator "are you sure?" / "are you checking actual code?" → STOP do code analysis). Evidence: v5.15.5.F.4d.1.B.4 v1.7.6 cycle Path 1 → Path 2 → Path 2 v3 → Path 2 v4 flip-flopping proved planning-time audit re-fire missing as structural enforcement. /precoding-audit-gate SKILL.md WHEN-TO-USE expanded with substantive-amendment trigger; CLAUDE.md "How to..." table has dedicated row.
- **Suggest mid-sprint audits when work impacts downstream** (2026-05-10). Trigger: HIGH-RISK ship just shipped / first pattern application / cross-cutting changes → suggest `/test-strength-audit` + `/dod-audit` + `/parity-check`; wait for greenlight.
- **Sub-plan sidecar files for substantial sections with implementation code samples** (2026-05-16) — convention: `<plan-name>-examples.md`. Trigger: section spans multi-file coordination OR architectural decision points OR >100 LOC OR new framework pattern → create sidecar.
- **Each DESIGN_SPECS doc has a CLAUDE.md cross-ref** (2026-05-09). Format: `Pattern documented in DESIGN_SPECS/<name>.md.` at end of relevant CLAUDE.md item.
- **Codify design principles in CLAUDE.md as patterns mature** (2026-05-09). Promote to CLAUDE.md once: ≥2 codebase applications OR DESIGN_SPECS doc exists, AND pattern is broad.
- **Auto-pick the more future-oriented design option when trade-off is clear** (2026-05-17) — `feedback_auto_pick_future_oriented.md`. Surface ONLY when (a) future-vs-now trade-off genuinely sharp OR (b) I genuinely don't know which is more future-oriented. Never punt with "your call" framing on auto-decidable decisions.
- **Audit → update → implement → ship cycle PER sub-ship** (2026-05-17). Trigger: each sub-ship in multi-sub-ship umbrella → `/precoding-audit-gate` → triage + consult → update plan → implement → ship + postmortem. Bank rest as TECH_DEBT.
- **Plans introducing new registries cite existing sister registry inspection** (2026-05-17) — `feedback_plans_cite_sister_registry_inspection.md`; `/readiness` Check 29. Trigger: plan proposes new registry/bit/dispatch/sidecar/macro → MUST include "Canonical sister registries considered" header section with per-candidate verdict.
- **Anti-spaghetti audit on cadence** (2026-05-17) — `project_anti_spaghetti_audit_cadence.md`. Trigger: quarterly codebase-wide run + post-new-anti-pattern-codification sweep + ad-hoc.
- **New plans use future-oriented plan template** (2026-05-17) — `feedback_new_plans_use_future_oriented_template.md`; `DESIGN_SPECS/plan-templates/future-oriented-plan-template.md`. Required sections: Design space + future-oriented choice / Canonical sister registries considered / Bug classes this closes / DESIGN_SPECs landed-amended / Verification gate / TECH_DEBT auto-write / Pre-coding triggers.
- **Plans + sub-plans codify explicit end goals** (2026-05-18) — `feedback_plans_have_explicit_end_goal.md`; `DESIGN_SPECS/plan-templates/future-oriented-plan-template.md` § End goal + `DESIGN_SPECS/plan-templates/sprint-master-plan-template.md`. Trigger: drafting MASTER plan / sub-plan / handoff. MASTER plan = "Sprint end goal" + per-sub-ship end goal column + sprint-end verification criteria. Sub-plan = "Ship end goal" (1-sentence: what surface is closed / what capability delivered) + acceptance criteria (CLOSED bug classes / CLOSED TECH_DEBT / LANDED DESIGN_SPECs / hot-path-untouched verification) + "how this contributes to sprint MASTER goal" tie-back. Handoffs cite both.

### Docs & files

- **New docs default to private** (2026-05-06). Trigger: doc captures unshipped direction / optimization findings / operator-edge / private cfgs → write to `plans/`. Public architectural-only → `DOCS/`. Auto-private patterns: `*_AUDIT.md`, `FUTURE_*.md`, `*-design-notes.md`, `*-hft-*.md`, `*-OPTIMIZATION-*.md`, `*-plan-check.md`, `STRATEGY_AND_CODING_RULES.md`, `GEMINI*.md`, `*.local.md`.
- **Workspace mirror for edge content** (2026-05-06) — `/sync-workspace` skill is canonical. Mirrors plans/, .claude/skills/ (symlinked); engine.cfg / backtest.cfg / controller.cfg / secrets.cfg / .env* / *.local.md (explicit copy).
- **Cold-pickup plan completeness — 10 fields** (2026-05-06) — `/readiness` Cold-pickup section is canonical. Branch / exec-order / Step-0 / function-names / file:line refs / stale-claim audit / effort-vs-LOC / source-audit paths / predecessor paths / tag+rollback anchors.
- **Doc layer separation: always-loaded vs on-demand** (2026-05-18) — `feedback_claude_md_guidelines_not_stuff_to_do.md`; `CLAUDE.md § Design philosophy` (Doc layer separation table). Trigger: editing CLAUDE.md / CLAUDE.local.md / MEMORY.md / SKILL.md → content must be TIMELESS (guidelines + categorical triggers + cross-ref pointers); sprint-specific TODO/version content goes in TECH_DEBT or plans. Drift sentinels: "queued as v5.X.Y sub-ship", "(NEW post-v5.X.Y)", "Recent <thing>" wording, specific TECH_DEBT-NNN in trigger bodies that should be categorical pattern triggers.
- **Categorical triggers > hardcoded refs in always-loaded content** (2026-05-18) — `feedback_categorical_triggers_over_hardcoded_refs.md`; `DESIGN_SPECS/doc-disciplines/categorical-triggers-in-always-loaded-docs.md`. Trigger: writing SKILL.md WHAT/WHEN trigger sections OR going-forward-rule body → use categorical pattern triggers ("any X-macro registry consumer template", "any wire-format-emitting code") instead of hardcoded refs (specific function names, specific TECH_DEBT-NNN, specific file paths). Stable catalog IDs (Class N, H N, M N, DESIGN_SPECS pattern names) KEEP. Worked examples KEEP with "(WORKED EXAMPLE)" framing. Sister: `feedback_claude_md_guidelines_not_stuff_to_do` (doc-layer separation; this is the categorical-vs-hardcoded axis).
- **Universal YAML frontmatter discipline for cross-referenced docs** (2026-05-18) — `DESIGN_SPECS/meta-disciplines/doc-frontmatter-convention.md`; `DESIGN_SPECS/meta-disciplines/doc-tag-vocabulary.md`. Trigger: creating any doc > 50 lines OR cross-referenced from other docs → add frontmatter per `doc-frontmatter-convention.md` (type / stage / version / established / tags / surface / sister_specs). Use tags from `doc-tag-vocabulary.md` CONCERN axis + SURFACE axis; lifecycle stage from 6-stage progression. Skill `/doc-create <type>` (queued at `.C` candidate ship per TECH_DEBT-115) scaffolds frontmatter from `design-spec-template.md` / `postmortem-template.md`. CI tool `check_doc_metadata.py` (queued) validates at commit time. Sister: `feedback_categorical_triggers_over_hardcoded_refs` (companion: WHAT SHAPE triggers take); `feedback_claude_md_guidelines_not_stuff_to_do` (companion: WHERE content goes); `feedback_metadata_audit_quarterly` (quarterly enforcement cadence).
- **Quarterly /metadata-audit cadence** (2026-05-18) — `feedback_metadata_audit_quarterly.md`. Trigger: quarterly cadence (sister to `/anti-spaghetti`) OR post-codification sweep OR operator-flagged finding-issues. Reports: missing frontmatter / undefined tags / broken sister-doc links / Stage 2 DRAFTs older than N sprints / singleton tags / filesystem-path mismatches. Skill QUEUED at `.C` candidate ship per TECH_DEBT-115 Phase 2; interim workflow is manual `rg` via CLAUDE.md § How to find anything.
- **File-size split discipline** (2026-05-18; RESCOPED 2026-05-27 per AI-driven solo workflow C1) — `feedback_file_size_split_discipline.md`; `DESIGN_SPECS/doc-disciplines/file-size-split-discipline.md` v1.4. **RESCOPED:** discipline applies SELECTIVELY in AI-driven solo workflow. Test 5K rule RETAINED for test-reliability concern. Source/header/plan/SKILL/DESIGN_SPECS/ledger thresholds become GUIDELINES not mandates (AI 1M context handles 6K-line files trivially; no human code-review cognitive load concern; compile time unchanged for header-only template code). Subfolder pattern (`.B.6` first canonical) stays Stage 3 frozen for future cohort use if human contributors join project OR AI tooling changes meaningfully. TECH_DEBT-029/-114/-116/-117/-118 CLOSED at `.B.7` as `wontfix-per-ai-workflow` (TECH_DEBT-117 closed as `done-incidentally`; TECH_DEBT-127 stays open as test-reliability surface). Original threshold table for reference: always-loaded docs 600 / tests 5000 / source headers 1500 / source bodies 2000 / ledgers 2000 / SKILL.md 1500 / DESIGN_SPECS 1200 / plans 1200 / memory 500 — most are now guidelines per scoping.
- **Registry default = single source of truth for cfg defaults** (2026-05-19) — `DESIGN_SPECS/framework-patterns/universal-cfg-field-registry-pattern.md` § Registry default precedence over manual defaults (v1.1 amendment). Trigger: any new cfg field row with default value column in FOREACH_*_CFG_FIELD registry → registry payload-default is canonical single source of truth; manual default initializer in struct body FORBIDDEN once registry has default. Per-row resolution at sweep: MATCH → delete manual; DIFFER → operator decision (update registry to match manual OR keep manual + document exemption at memory file). Sister: `feedback_no_defer_for_effort` (parent meta-rule); `feedback_structural_fix_for_recurring_class` (registry-as-single-source-of-truth IS the structural fix); `autopopulate-pattern-for-production-caller-class.md` (same N-site → 1-site closure shape applied to default-value surface). Closes registry-vs-manual default drift class.

### Operator collaboration

- **Address Caramel as Caramel / she / her** (`feedback_address_user_as_caramel.md`).
- **No AskUserQuestion modal boxes** — present options inline (`feedback_no_question_boxes.md`).
- **Evaluate options on robustness + latency + design philosophy, NOT time** (`feedback_evaluate_options_on_robustness_latency_design_not_time.md`).
- **After pre-coding checks, ALWAYS consult before coding** (`feedback_consult_on_audit_findings.md`).
- **Defer is last-ditch, never effort-avoidance** (`feedback_no_defer_for_effort.md`).
- **Compaction degrades — verify handoffs against current code** (`feedback_compaction_degrades_treat_handoffs_as_hints.md`).
- **Motivated collaborator for Caramel** — work mindset (`feedback_motivated_collaborator_for_caramel.md`). Public AGPL + hedge fund attention + exacting standards = high quality bar. When tempted to shortcut, pick the path that produces the best software.
- **Backwards compat NOT a default concern** (2026-05-26; REFINED 2026-05-26 PM) — `feedback_backwards_compat_not_default_concern.md`. Trigger: refactor / deletion / cleanup scope proposals. OSS personal tool; default to cleanest architectural answer (full surface deletion, no preserve-and-deprecate layer). Operator flags explicitly when load-bearing exceptions apply (stamp body / persistence / model handle ABI / locked cfg semantics). Codified at `.B.4` v1.7.5 D18 — `engine_arch=centralized` SHARDED deprecation scope simplified from "preserve + REFUSE" to "full surface delete" per operator preference. **REFINEMENT (2026-05-26 PM at WIP-12 per /readiness G1 CRITICAL):** Operator migration impact SECTION is REQUIRED even when backwards compat NOT preserved. SECTION captures REASONING + categorization (who's affected; what happens post-deletion; sister-architectural preservation surface if any). PATH (actual preserve-and-deprecate implementation) is OPTIONAL per this rule's exceptions list. SECTION ≠ PATH. Sister: `feedback_no_defer_for_effort` + `feedback_motivated_collaborator_for_caramel` + `feedback_surface_operator_migration_path_proactively` (sister rule that REFINEMENT clarifies — section ALWAYS required; path optional per exceptions list).

